    "story": "The helmet was new enough to still hold its shape. The netting had been tied by hands that knew why it mattered, and he had not touched it since — like a man who has said his prayers and means not to say them twice.\nHe kept his eyes on the line where the field turned to sky. Something out there had already been decided, and the rest was walking. The strap across his chest had stopped biting somewhere around the third mile.\nThe order, when it came, would only tell him what his eyes already knew.",
