    "description": "A painterly World War II portrait of a young soldier in a mud-splattered raincoat and helmet, standing in the rain in soft, muted light. Grounded in WWII reenactment photography and historical authenticity, this World War II fine art photograph captures the quiet endurance of the Greatest Generation in the wet hours of the war, where resolve is carried in a soaked coat rather than in words. This wartime portrait photography piece explores heroic portraits not through combat, but through the steady patience of a man who has learned to outlast the weather. Part of Wayne Heim's *Facing History* fine art photography series. © Wayne Heim",
