    "description": "A painterly World War II portrait of a British tank crewman in a black beret with his goggles pushed up, a camouflage smock and a scarf at his throat, his rifle carried over one shoulder against a weathered stone wall. His weathered face holds a wry, unflinching look — the look of a man used to the close air inside steel and the dust of the road outside it. Part of Wayne Heim's *Facing History* fine art photography series. © Wayne Heim",
